  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "S.Gayathri vs The District Collector on 18 March, 2025",
    "facts": "This Writ Petition has been filed seeking for issuance of a Writ of Certiorarified Mandamus, to call for the records in connection with the impugned order passed by the second respondent in his proceedings in Na.Ka.No.1497/2023/Ka(1), dated 23.11.2023 and quash the same and consequently direct the respondents to extend the benefits of the jewels loan waiver scheme vide G.O.Ms.No.97(Co-operative Society Food and Consumer Safety Department(CC1), dated 01.11.2021 by returning the jewels to the petitioner under the Jewel Loan.no.4019 on the file of the 3 rd respondent, within the stipulated time. He further submitted that since waiver under the above said scheme was not granted to the petitioner, she approached the District Level Grievance Committee. After re-measurement of the said jewels, it was 40.250 milli grams and the same was mentioned in the impugned order passed by the second respondent vide Na.No.1497/2023/A(1) dated 23.11.2023. The learned counsel placed reliance on the judgment of the First Bench of this Court in Writ Appeal no.927 of 2024 dated 20.03.2024 in the case of The President, Gingee Primary Agricultural Co-operative Credit Society, Gingee, Villupuram District versus A.Shanthi and others. In that case, the petitioner therein, pledged the jewels on 27.10.2021. At the time of pledging, it was about 40 grams of net weight and when the same was remeasured , it was about 40.500 milli grams. On that ground, the petitioner was held to be dis-entitled for the benefits extended under the jewel loan waiver scheme and hence, she approached this Court in W.P.No.23900 of 2023 and a learned single Judge of this Court has allowed the Writ Petition. Challenging the said order, the appellant/society has filed the Writ Appeal. The admitted position is that the first respondent availed the loan on 27.1.2021 by pledging her jewels. At the time when the jewels were pledged, the appellant issued a receipt stating that the gross weight of the pledged jewels is 40 grams and the net weight is 34 grams. It appears that, thereafter, the government issued G.O.Ms.No.97, dated 1.11.2021, extending the benefit of jewel loan waiver scheme to the members of the cooperative society. The benefit was given to those borrowers who had pledged the jewels weighing up to 40 grams. 7. The first respondent sought to avail the benefit of the said government order.",
